course: dictionary
lesson: 7688
title: Working out a hard dinosaur word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Protoceratops» is a long, hard word, but the sentences around it give you clues. «The fighting dinosaurs fossil shows a Velociraptor and a Protoceratops buried mid-fight» tells you it is a dinosaur, and that it was caught in a fight.
explain: The dictionary tells you more: it was a small plant-eating dinosaur, about the size of a sheep, with a parrot-like beak and a bony frill at the back of its head. Check each new clue against this picture, and see if it fits.
explain: Some words hide in the sentence. «Some historians think ancient people who found Protoceratops skulls in the Gobi Desert imagined griffins.» Ancient means very old, so these people lived long ago, and the skulls are not from today. Read the words around a word to find out who or what it is about.
fact: Protoceratops is a noun, and it is spelled the same for one animal or many.
fact: Protoceratops was a small plant-eating dinosaur, about the size of a sheep.
fact: Protoceratops lived about 75 million years ago, in Mongolia and China.
fact: Protoceratops was an early relative of Triceratops, but it had no big horns.
fact: Some people think Protoceratops skulls may have helped start the griffin legend, but this is an idea, not something proven.
exercise: «A real fossil shows a Velociraptor and a Protoceratops locked in a fight.» What is a fossil? | A modern bird | *The preserved remains or traces of a living thing from long ago | A kind of sand dune | A toy dinosaur
exercise: Protoceratops had a parrot-like beak and a bony frill. What was the frill? | A set of big horns | A long, thin neck | *A bony shield at the back of its head | A feathered tail
exercise: «Some historians think ancient people who found Protoceratops skulls in the Gobi Desert imagined griffins.» Which word means very old? | Historians | *Ancient | Skulls | Griffins
test: About how big was Protoceratops? | *About the size of a sheep | A cat | About the size of an elephant | About the size of a turkey
test: The sentence says the griffin idea is «an idea, not something proven.» What does proven mean? | *Shown to be true | Small | Painted | Lost
exam: Which clue in the lessons shows Protoceratops ate plants? | It lived in a desert | It was found in a fight | *It was a plant-eating dinosaur | It had feathers like a Velociraptor
